  "result": "Excellent! All 155 tests pass. I've successfully implemented a comprehensive date utility module with UTC-based date operations. Here's what was added:\n\n**New src/dates.js module with three functions:**\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`** - Validates date strings:\n   - Checks YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Verifies the date is real (catches invalid dates like 2024-02-30)\n   - Works in UTC\n   - Returns boolean\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`** - Adds days to a date:\n   - Input: date string in YYYY-MM-DD format, number of days\n   - Handles positive and negative offsets\n   - Correctly handles month/year boundaries\n   - Properly handles leap years\n   - Returns date string in YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - All arithmetic in UTC\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`** - Calculates days between two dates:\n   - Input: two date strings in YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Returns whole days: b - a\n   - Handles negative differences\n   - All calculations in UTC\n   - Correctly handles leap years\n\n**Updates to createInvoice():**\n- Now imports and uses `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed duplicate `isValidDate` function\n\n**Comprehensive tests (38 new tests):**\n- `isValidDate`: valid dates, invalid dates, wrong format, leap year handling\n- `addDays`: positive/negative offsets, month boundaries, year boundaries, leap years, large offsets\n- `daysBetween`: positive/negative differences, month/year boundaries, leap years, large ranges, roundtrip verification\n- Integration tests verifying all functions work together in UTC\n\nAll date operations are strictly UTC-based\u2014no local timezone conversions, ensuring consistent behavior across machines and regions.",
